      "message": "test(ui): pin the Bore ring plan in the detect-holes note tests\n\nPR #1839 (#1566) lets Bore clear a wide hole with concentric rings, so\nDetect holes keeps the Ø74.3 hole that the two UI tests expected it to\nskip. The product is right and the tests were stale.\n\nThe tests now use a Ø10 bull-nose with a 4.999 mm corner. A Ø74.3\nthrough hole is stored (14 rings). A Ø24 blind hole needs 8750 rings\nat its flat floor, past the 4096 budget: it is skipped by name, and a\nplate with only that hole is refused and stores nothing. The fixture\nbuilder now takes a blind floor height per cell.\n\nFixes #1909\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
